From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Osterloh <richard.osterloh@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:31:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mgmt: hawkbit: fix resuming from a full or ignored range

Progress saved at 100% (a reboot between the last chunk and the hash
check) made every later attempt send "Range: bytes=<size>-", which the
server cannot satisfy, so the download failed on every poll and the
saved progress was never cleared.

When the server answers 200 instead of 206, bytes_written was reset but
erased_up_to kept the value loaded with the progress, so the pages
below it were written without being erased and the hash check failed.

Signed-off-by: Richard Osterloh <richard.osterloh@gmail.com>
---
 subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c b/subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c
index 7b0aee795..6f7c65e4f 100644
--- a/subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c
+++ b/subsys/mgmt/hawkbit/hawkbit.c
@@ -997,7 +997,13 @@ static void response_download_cb(struct http_response *rsp, enum http_final_call
 		hb_context->dl.http_content_size = rsp->content_length;
 		download_progress = 0;
 		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAWKBIT_SAVE_PROGRESS) && rsp->http_status_code != 206) {
+			/* Restarting from 0: the erase state loaded with the
+			 * progress would skip erasing the pages below it.
+			 */
 			hb_context->flash_ctx.stream.bytes_written = 0;
+#ifdef CONFIG_STREAM_FLASH_ERASE
+			hb_context->flash_ctx.stream.erased_up_to = 0;
+#endif
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -1160,7 +1166,11 @@ static bool send_request(struct hawkbit_context *hb_context, enum hawkbit_http_r
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_HAWKBIT_SAVE_PROGRESS
 		hb_context->dl.downloaded_size = flash_img_bytes_written(&hb_context->flash_ctx);
-		if (IN_RANGE(hb_context->dl.downloaded_size, 1, hb_context->dl.file_size)) {
+		/* Progress saved at 100% (reboot before the hash check) gets a full
+		 * download: "Range: bytes=<size>-" is unsatisfiable and would fail
+		 * every attempt.
+		 */
+		if (IN_RANGE(hb_context->dl.downloaded_size, 1, hb_context->dl.file_size - 1)) {
 			snprintf(header_range, sizeof(header_range), "Range: bytes=%u-" HTTP_CRLF,
 				 hb_context->dl.downloaded_size);
 
-- 
